{"title":"Ireland fact of the day","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/919898684/0/marginalrevolution~Ireland-fact-of-the-day.html","date":1749366268000,"content":"<blockquote><p>Ireland’s population are the most educated in the world — with 52.4% (1.8million) of the population aged between 25-64 having a bachelor’s degree or higher.</p>\r\n<p>While, of course, the whole numbers of people with bachelors degrees may be higher in countries with a higher number of people, percentage wise Ireland is the most educated; beating out countries such as Switzerland (46%), Singapore (45%), Belgium (44.1%) and the UK (43.6%) who round out the top five.</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>Here is<a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://extra.ie/2025/05/30/news/most-educated-countries-ireland\" target=\"_blank\"> the link</a>.  That would not have been an obvious prediction say in the 1970s.  Here is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://chatgpt.com/share/684475f8-c17c-8010-abce-881324b34d58\" target=\"_blank\">o3 on how this came about</a>.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/06/ireland-fact-of-the-day-7.html\">Ireland fact of the day</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/919898684/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/919898684/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/919898684/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/919898684/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.c